15 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating how hyperglycemia induces factors such as hypoxia, oxidative stress, inflammation, ER stress, autophagy, apoptosis, and fibrosis, which affect kidney function. Zinc ions are shown influencing various signaling pathways that contribute to preventive and renoprotective effects for the kidney, with pathways including TGF-beta/Smads, PI3K/AKT, Nrf2, NF-kB, Wnt/beta-catenin, HIF-1 alpha/VEGF, RAGE, TNFAIP3, GSK-3 beta, HIF-1 alpha, mTORC1, and ERK/MAPK.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Diagram of a cell showing insulin secretion, glucose transport, and zinc ion movement through ZnT and ZIP transporters at various locations, including the plasma membrane, endoplasmic reticulum, and Golgi apparatus.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Biological diagram illustrating zinc ions activating GPR39 on the cell membrane, leading to signaling via ERK/MAPK and PI3K/AKT pathways and resulting in insulin secretion. Membrane channels include VDCC for calcium influx, NHE1 for sodium and hydrogen exchange, NKCC1 for chloride, sodium, and potassium transport, and NCX for sodium-calcium exchange. GABA-A receptors mediate chloride influx, and organelles labeled AG and ER are depicted, showing calcium uptake and release. Red arrows indicate activation and depolarization processes.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating insulin signaling through ERK/MAPK and PIP3/AKT pathways, showing components like insulin receptor, gene expression, mTOR C1, GLUT4, zinc ions, and outputs including glucose transport and glycogen synthesis.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Illustration compares acute and chronic hypoxia effects. Acute hypoxia increases angiogenesis and erythropoietin expression while reducing oxidative stress, inflammation, apoptosis, mitochondrial autophagy, fibrosis, and vascular calcification. Chronic hypoxia results in reactive oxygen species, podocyte apoptosis, pro-inflammatory cytokines, NLRP3 activation, extracellular matrix accumulation, and renal fibrosis.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt <> /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
